  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v26.9.0 - rendering and cross-platform release.\n\nNew: PdfFileSanitization repairs files too damaged to load (header/EOF waste, broken cross-reference table); DateField form fields; HideAction; ruby and warichu tagged-structure elements with the StructureTypeStandard role set; a composite drawing Path shape; typed exceptions for empty values, forbidden font embedding, signature-length mismatch and missing optional dependencies (the printing guard names the package to add).\nRendering: dash patterns on software strokes, soft masks (matte, backdrop, isolated/non-isolated groups), colour-key masks, overprint and multi-spot ink spaces, tiling-pattern ranges, function-based shadings, indexed images with soft masks, DPI-exact output, annotations rotating with the page, sub-pixel-thin images.\nText: horizontal scaling and negative sizes flip and stretch glyphs, vertical CMaps, substitute faces for fonts without a program, CJK radical fallback, whole-paragraph re-flow on replace.\nCross-platform: managed BMP/JPEG/TIFF paths, font fallback by name, case-blind and Windows-authored asset paths, glyph recognition, redaction and image colour sampling all work off Windows.\nAlso: PDF 2.0 saves move descriptive Info text into XMP and write non-Latin-1 text as UTF-16BE; PDF/A conversion refuses live-signed files and exempts freshly UA-converted documents from the untagged-content scan; signature trust reads intermediates from the per-user store; action Next chains and submit targets; XMP structs stay live; forms treat a field as the collection of its widgets; plus HTML-to-PDF, generator table, facade and annotation fixes.\n\nFull release notes: https://github.com/aspose-pdf-foss/Aspose.PDF-FOSS-for-.NET/releases/tag/v26.9.0",
